\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.2}{\ignorespaces VaR marks where the worst days begin, and expected shortfall measures how bad they are. VaR and expected shortfall for normal returns. The shaded tail holds the worst 1\% of days. The 99\% VaR, 2.33 standard deviations below zero, marks where that tail begins. The 99\% ES, 2.67 standard deviations, is the average loss on the days in the tail, so it is always larger than the VaR.}}{124}{figure.caption.33}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:11-var-es}{{8.2}{124}{VaR marks where the worst days begin, and expected shortfall measures how bad they are. VaR and expected shortfall for normal returns. The shaded tail holds the worst 1\% of days. The 99\% VaR, 2.33 standard deviations below zero, marks where that tail begins. The 99\% ES, 2.67 standard deviations, is the average loss on the days in the tail, so it is always larger than the VaR}{figure.caption.33}{}}
